Alembic migrations for Driftwatch.

The application runs `alembic upgrade head` on startup (see
`driftwatch.db.Database.upgrade`), so a fresh database is built and an existing
one is migrated forward automatically. A database first created by an older
`create_all` build is adopted by stamping it to head before upgrading.

To add a migration after changing the models:

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"
    # review the generated file in versions/, then
    alembic upgrade head

`env.py` reads the database URL from the application's settings and maps the
async driver to its synchronous peer, so no URL needs to be set in alembic.ini.
For PostgreSQL, install a sync driver (`psycopg`) alongside `asyncpg`.
